#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:5
#: 8393083ca6494572a8e2cf1b6b4832ed
msgid "Video Transmitter Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:7
#: ba48ddacbad649d398c17e0b92d2c79a
msgid "Video transmitter (VTX) support allows the autopilot to control an attached video transmitter. Depending on the VTX and protocol used, components that can be controlled include video band, video channel, transmitter power and pit mode. Supported protocols are SmartAudio, IRC Tramp, and TBS Crossfire (CRSF)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:9
#: db334f91cc714d4695e090435dde43bc
msgid "Not all video transmitters claiming SmartAudio support fully support the specification and some functions may not be provided in that transmitter, or implemented in a non-standard way. Consult the manufacturer's documentation if questions arise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:12
#: 5ed204b7e74b4e7b98acd39a64a99e26
msgid "How to setup video transmitter support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:14
#: 7de6b50e39c94f95b5b3003de9750b25
msgid "To enable video transmitter support you need to set the following parameters and reboot your autopilot:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:16
#: 2b91ab844f83451eabe478fde30ca4c7
msgid "Set :ref:`VTX_ENABLE <VTX_ENABLE>` to 1 to enable video transmitter support. Although this enables support it will not achieve anything without an appropriate video transmitter protocol enabled, as described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:19
#: 3ff5be4050b64c62bbca6f0dd0146210
msgid "SmartAudio"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:21
#: bc514e62c9004bd2972a5e50331fd0f8
msgid "SmartAudio is a one-wire protocol so you will need to connect the SmartAudio pin of your VTX to the TX pin of the serial port you want to use. You will also need to make sure your VTX is configured for SmartAudio control. For example if attached to SERIAL port 5:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:23
#: 4245d270728b47cf8dd7f12c4888a519
msgid "Set :ref:`SERIAL5_PROTOCOL <SERIAL5_PROTOCOL>` to 37 to enable SmartAudio."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:24
#: dcfb9cb5dfc34996a4d2061a2b141d4c
msgid "Set :ref:`SERIAL5_OPTIONS <SERIAL5_OPTIONS>` to 4 to enable half-duplex which SmartAudio requires. Depending on your video transmitter it might be required to enable the TX_PullDown option, so 68 would be the correct value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:25
#: c06ee705027f4868a9b3c7c349d5c3f4
msgid "Set :ref:`SERIAL5_BAUD <SERIAL5_BAUD>` to 4800 to set the SmartAudio baud rate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:31
#: 69cb2100f8884b849f2b831da9c225de
msgid "CRSF (Crossfire)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:33
#: d2d679720d4f487991d3cc66b5f0fbad
msgid "CRSF is a bi-directional protocol that requires both TX and RX of a serial port to be connected. Follow the instructions for CRSF telemetry to setup CRSF support (See :ref:`common-tbs-rc`). If you only wish to use CRSF for VTX support, then (again using SERIAL5 as an example) :ref:`SERIAL5_PROTOCOL <SERIAL5_PROTOCOL>` should be set to 29 rather than 23. You will also need to make sure your VTX is configured for CRSF control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:35
#: edb145daebbc4d4a8439afd54d16c640
msgid "When using CRSF for both RC/Telem and VTX control it is important to disable \"my VTX\" support on Open TX transmitters. Follow your transmitters' instructions. In this scenario, you must connect your autopilot's UART to your CRSF receiver, and then connect your CRSF receiver to the VTX to forward CRSF commands, you cannot connect to the FC using CRSF directly for both the Receiver and VTX using two UARTs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:37
#: d769a7e47cda4cee89543064d1811215
msgid "Reboot your autopilot and power your video transmitter. At startup you should see a video message indicating the current video settings. All the video settings are stored in the ``VTX_x`` parameters and by default these will be changed to reflect the currently configured VTX settings. Once booted you can modify these settings and they will be reflected in the VTX configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:48
#: 7c492602d0e34043b37cdca9945cdd7a
msgid "ImmersionRC Tramp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:50
#: 506e80177f364c7283f0c9f720253ee1
msgid "Connect the telemetry pin of the video transmitter to the TX pin of the autopilot's UART used to control it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:51
#: 6fed135d51aa4bcba065a225e2d613d1
msgid "Set :ref:`SERIAL5_PROTOCOL <SERIAL5_PROTOCOL>` = 44 if using SERIAL5 for connection to VTX"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:54
#: 151642ff0ebc44f588dfcadcf3573b8d
msgid "Video transmitter settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:56
#: 56edecd020324358abc3ae9ff38e15be
msgid "Set :ref:`VTX_BAND <VTX_BAND>` to modify the VTX band."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:57
#: ac698fab9770479895f09ceac9f0590d
msgid "Set :ref:`VTX_CHANNEL <VTX_CHANNEL>` to modify the VTX channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:58
#: b1e783f763e140d98b4a9f3e7b0f7c90
msgid "Set :ref:`VTX_FREQ <VTX_FREQ>` to modify the VTX frequency. Band/channel and frequency are mutually exclusive, if you set band and/or channel then the frequency will be automatically updated. If you set the frequency then the band/channel will be automatically updated. Not all frequencies, channels and bands are supported unless the transmitter is unlocked. Please consult local regulations before doing this. If you select an unsupported frequency then the current frequency will not be changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:59
#: 9f16ed63563a47a89e38f02eb532beb9
msgid "Set :ref:`VTX_POWER <VTX_POWER>` to modify the VTX power in mw. Not all transmitters support all power values. In particular in Europe only 25mw is allowed by default. To allow other values the transmitter must be unlocked. If you select a power level that is unsupported by the transmitter then the actual power value will not be changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:60
#: 659f1a16f34a4ea081c797245a51f2e0
msgid "Set :ref:`VTX_MAX_POWER <VTX_MAX_POWER>` to set the maximum VTX power allowed in mw. This is used by ``RCx_OPTION`` = 94 which allows the VTX power to be changed via a switch or dial."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:61
#: d0f8dcf3867a4239a152cd65618547ab
msgid "Set :ref:`VTX_OPTIONS <VTX_OPTIONS>` to set options on the VTX. The most common option is setting bit 0 which puts the VTX into pit mode, if supported. Other options can be used to reset pitmode upon arming and/or set it upon disarming (bits 1 and 2). The option bits and their actions are shown below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:64
#: e861a362b3644a3a89ecc93f7335e421
msgid ":ref:`VTX_OPTIONS<VTX_OPTIONS>` bit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:64
#: f75cd98d3dd94a89af698563dcbdd6c1
msgid "Function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:66
#: 21b9b1fd238345c5ac0a7f5e27f2aee1
msgid "0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:66
#: 211d5192492940ebb135f65083329478
msgid "Directly sets VTX into PIT MODE, if available"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:67
#: d3e78d321a024c58918153a2d2332e68
msgid "1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:67
#: 339a056dc24446ec8b56c35c74320d32
msgid "Resets bit 0 above upon arming"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:68
#: 7317d96ee06142feb1cf685eccbd97f6
msgid "2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:68
#: 411f542afc5d47fa90dd74bbc04b797e
msgid "Sets bit 0 above upon disarming"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:69
#: 9abd0cb1ac4c4285a736c66769d1aa9b
msgid "3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:69
#: d03bb9eeb15a4f3e9e9735053ff5190c
msgid "Unlock: unlocks frequencies and bands on some transmitters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:70
#: e096b6b7fce44d7fac0cabb56fe51719
msgid "4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:70
#: 4e476b80535944609f6f42d94104e3c8
msgid "Add leading zero byte to requests (needed on some transmitters)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:71
#: 3501a57698ea494cacac9f48b1676e33
msgid "5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:71
#: a599f87f4fd74ec3b01d02bb0ce5475e
msgid "Use 1 stop bit. Needed for some transmitters using non-compliant(iNAV) messaging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:72
#: e7a05fac5f9044619b7d11533d6f8f1e
msgid "6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:72
#: 5f4ce2f33c644e248e2fbe91c29825e3
msgid "Ignore CRC checks. Needed for some transmitters using non-compliant messaging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:73
#: b392aa2cbe6341f69d2d265ec9b9004e
msgid "7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:73
#: e108b16d967241db9bfca58991872941
msgid "Future (not presently working)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:76
#: 7b31e0f26c3b4c3bb03790482b4c1a4f
msgid "\"unlocking\" can be done differently, depending on transmitter brand. Also, using unlocked frequencies/power levels may violate local laws and restrictions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:79
#: b521449ea5654b2da9a492e543f37e05
msgid "Setting video transmitter settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:81
#: 681a9de5c03e47f6af9fb0049189590a
msgid "Video transmitter settings can be changed in multiple ways but always go via the ``VTX_x`` parameters. So any option which advertises VTX control will be setting a ``VTX_x`` parameter which in turn will interface with the protocol backends. Here are the current ways that video transmitter settings can be modified:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:83
#: a6813a40e9e748e7969728d1c8b6ec4e
msgid "Parameter modification through your ground station"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vtx.rst:84
#: 5923f60c93894415bdfedae7b9431a15
msgid "Transmitter power via RC switch (``RCx_OPTION`` = 94). With this setting, the RC channel is interpreted as a 6-position switch (dividing the PWM range 1200 to 1800), and then this is assigned to power values based on the ``VTX_MAX_POWER``. For example if max power is 200-499mW, switch positions 0 results in 0mw (pit mode), 1 and 2 result in 25mw, 3 and 4 result in 100mw, and 5 results in 200mw."
msgstr ""

